{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"starving-sphalerite-skua","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\nWith the tame-melodious-veery performance fix, enforced `verify-identity --all` (`REBAR_IDENTITY_REQUIRE_AUTHENTICATED=1`, no `enforce_since`) now completes on a fresh no-remote TMPDIR clone of `origin/tickets` b878d77e28d (310,079 commits) in 26 min 7 s. It exits 1:\n\n`42612 verified, 874 unsigned, 0 unknown-author, 7007 bad-signature, 0 key-not-valid-at-era (50493 event(s) in scope)`\n\nAll 7,007 bad-signature verdicts are SNAPSHOT `authorship_ledger` entries (1,018 tickets); no live event is bad-signature. This is the ORIGINAL, un-reclaimed history, so it is not a reclaim defect.\n\nLedger composition on that clone (44,311 entries), grouped by the SSHSIG public key embedded in each signature (sha256 prefix of the key blob) and by whether compaction recorded `signer_pubkey`:\n- key 3d4e271c8a89 (on identity 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d's keyring, added 1784000818…): 35,403 set, 1,301 null\n- key a060aace07c3 (on the keyring, added 1788820763…): 2,600 set, 19 null\n- key 6e2a8414bf53: 2,557, all null — NOT on any keyring record of 594c\n- key 61689bf468f5: 2,430, all null — NOT on any keyring record of 594c\n- key 0a2a4ec106e4: 1 set\n\n`_verify_signed` in `src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py` returns `bad-signature` for any ledger entry whose `signer_pubkey` is null, before trying a verify. So two classes are mixed:\n1. ~4,987 entries signed by two keys that the author identity's keyring never recorded (genuinely unverifiable against in-band keys; which hosts held those keys is not established).\n2. ~1,320 entries signed by keys that ARE on the keyring but recorded null at compaction (a random sample of 40 null entries: 4 verify against the current keyring via `identify_signer`, 36 do not). Likely compaction ran where the key was not yet on the keyring; not established.\nThe remaining ~700 bad-signature verdicts among `signer_pubkey`-set entries are not yet broken down.\n\n## Why it matters\nEpic polite-antivirus-bedbug's operator hold requires an enforced `verify-identity` that PASSES on the rewritten history before publication. It cannot pass on the rewritten history while it fails on the original. CI runs with `enforce_since` set, which grandfathers pre-anchor events, so the CI lane is not affected today.\n\n## Not established\n- Where keys 6e2a8414bf53 and 61689bf468f5 come from, and whether they should be registered on identity 594c (a keyring change is an operator decision about trust).\n- Whether the intended acceptance for the reclaim hold is \"enforced with the committed `enforce_since`\" or \"enforced with no boundary\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The origin of each bad-signature class is identified with evidence (keys and compaction hosts).\n- [ ] The remedy (keyring registration by the operator, re-identification of signers at verify time, or a documented grandfather boundary) is decided by the operator and implemented.\n- [ ] Enforced `verify-identity --all` on a fresh clone of origin/tickets reports 0 enforced not-verified events under the decided boundary.\n","id":"df01-290f-89a2-4ce8","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["identity","verify-identity"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Enforced verify-identity fails on the current tickets history: 7,007 SNAPSHOT ledger entries classify bad-signature"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795029251512550065,"uuid":"47c1b7e0-79c1-46d0-9241-c04653d87600"}